@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+.\"
+.\" This file and its contents are supplied under the terms of the
+.\" Common Development and Distribution License ("CDDL"), version 1.0.
+.\" You may only use this file in accordance with the terms of version
+.\" 1.0 of the CDDL.
+.\"
+.\" A full copy of the text of the CDDL should have accompanied this
+.\" source.  A copy of the CDDL is also available via the Internet at
+.\" http://www.illumos.org/license/CDDL.
+.\"
+.\"
+.\" Copyright 2026 isoriano1968
+.\"
+.Dd November 13, 2026
+.Dt SMCSTAT 8
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm smcstat
+.Nd show temperatures and fans of an Intel Mac
+.Sh SYNOPSIS
+.Nm
+.Op Fl ap
+.Op Fl i Ar secs
+.Op Ar key ...
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+The
+.Nm
+utility reads the System Management Controller of an Intel-based Apple
+Macintosh through
+.Xr applesmc 4D .
+Without options it lists every populated temperature key with its value in
+degrees Celsius and a short description where the key is known, followed by
+the fans with their current, target, minimum and maximum speed in RPM and
+the name the SMC gives them.
+.Pp
+With
+.Ar key
+arguments only those keys are shown, each with its type, length and value,
+decoded where the type is known and in hexadecimal otherwise.
+.Sh OPTIONS
+.Bl -tag -width Fl
+.It Fl a
+Show every key of the SMC.
+.It Fl i Ar secs
+Repeat every
+.Ar secs
+seconds.
+.It Fl p
+Parsable output, one colon-separated record per line:
+.Sm off
+.Sy temp : Ar key : Ar celsius
+.Sm on
+for temperatures,
+.Sm off
+.Sy fan : Ar n : Ar rpm : Ar target : Ar min : Ar max : Ar name
+.Sm on
+for fans
+.Pq \-1 where the SMC has no value ,
+and
+.Sm off
+.Ar key : Ar type : Ar value
+.Sm on
+for keys given as arguments or with
+.Fl a .
+.El
+.Sh FILES
+.Bl -tag -width Pa
+.It Pa /dev/applesmc
+SMC device.
+.El
+.Sh EXIT STATUS
+.Ex -std
+.Sh EXAMPLES
+.Bl -tag -width 0n
+.It Sy Example 1 No Temperatures and fans
+.Bd -literal
+$ smcstat
+.Ed
+.It Sy Example 2 No Two keys every five seconds
+.Bd -literal
+$ smcstat -i 5 TC0P F0Ac
+.Ed
+.El
+.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
+The command line is
+.Sy Uncommitted .
+The output is
+.Sy Not-An-Interface ,
+except with
+.Fl p ,
+which is
+.Sy Uncommitted .
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr applesmc 4D
